.TH FCCANALYSIS\-SUBMIT 1 "14 Sep 2026" "0.13.1" "fccanalysis-submit man page"

.SH NAME
\fBfccanalysis\-submit\fR \- submit FCC analysis to be run on a distributed system

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fccanalysis submit ht-condor
[\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR]
.I analysis-script
\fB\-\-\fR
[\fIANALYSIS ARGUMENTS\fR]
.PP
.B fccanalysis submit grid
[\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-\-lfn\-input\fR \fILFN_LIST\fR]
\fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT_FILE\fR
\fB\-\-output\-dir\fR \fIOUTPUT_DIR\fR
[\fB\-\-output\-se\fR \fISTORAGE_ELEMENT\fR]
[\fB\-\-files\-per\-job\fR \fICOUNT\fR | \fB\-\-n\-chunks\fR \fICOUNT\fR]
[\fB\-\-sample\-name\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-site\fR \fISITE\fR]
[\fB\-\-mode\fR {\fBwms\fR,\fBlocal\fR}]
[\fB\-\-ship\-local\-build\fR]
.I analysis-script
[\fB\-\-\fR \fIRUN ARGUMENTS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fccanalysis submit
submits the analysis defined by
.I analysis-script
to the selected backend.
The supported backends are CERN HTCondor and the DIRAC-managed grid.
Slurm is recognized but is not yet implemented.

.SS HTCondor
The mechanism of submission of the jobs to the HTCondor depends on the
filesystem which hosts the code of the FCCAnalyses. If the code is hosted on the
AFS the jobs are submitted using shared filesystem mechanism, otherwise spool
mechanism is used.

Here is an overview where the output of the jobs can be saved depending on
where the FCCAnalyses code is hosted:
.nf
  | Hosted on \\ Output to | AFS | EOS |
  | --------------------- | --- | --- |
  |                   AFS |  x  |  x  |
  |                   EOS |  0  |  x  |
.fi

.SS DIRAC grid
The grid backend first constructs the modern
.B Analysis
object from the analysis script, resolves and validates all selected inputs,
and creates a deterministic plan of independent jobs.
Each job receives the analysis script, its own generated input-file list, and
any optional analysis helpers or local FCCAnalyses build through its input
sandbox.

The submission helper is started in an isolated DIRAC client environment.
It reuses a valid DIRAC proxy or creates one for the configured DIRAC group.
In
.B wms
mode DIRAC sends the jobs to grid worker nodes; in
.B local
mode DIRAC executes them on the submission machine for testing.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B analysis-script
Path to the analysis script\&.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Prints short help message and exits\&.
.TP
.I ANALYSIS ARGUMENTS
Command line arguments which will not be parsed by the framework and will be
passed directly to the analysis script\&.

.SH GRID INPUT MODES
.SS XRootD input
This is the default grid input mode.
The backend reads
.B Analysis.samples
and resolves one per-sample input source (\fIinput-dir\fR,
\fIinput-files\fR, or \fIinput-file-list\fR), falling back to the global
\fBAnalysis.input_dir\fR when a sample has no source. Directories are listed
through XRootD and contribute immediate \fI.root\fR files only. The backend
then applies any sample fraction and divides the resulting file URLs into jobs.
Workers stream these files directly over XRootD.

Mounted \fI/eos/experiment/fcc/...\fR and \fI/eos/user/...\fR paths are
converted to CERN XRootD URLs. Other EOS namespaces and non-CERN storage must
use an explicit URL, for example
\fBroot://storage.example.org//data/events.root\fR. URLs ending in
\fI.root\fR name files; other URLs are treated as directories.

Grid jobs receive XRootD URLs, not files from the submitting machine. Local
paths are therefore rejected in XRootD input mode. This does not apply to
\fB--lfn-input\fR, which uses DIRAC staging instead.

.SS DIRAC LFN input
Supplying
.B --lfn-input
selects LFN mode.
The named text file must contain one absolute DIRAC logical file name per
non-empty line.
These are catalogue LFNs, not the physical paths or XRootD URLs used by a
sample's \fIinput-file-list\fR.
DIRAC stages each planned job's assigned input data into the worker directory,
and the generated per-job input-file list refers to the staged filenames.
Unless explicit grouping is requested, one LFN is assigned to each job.

.SH GRID OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-lfn\-input\fR \fILFN_LIST\fR
Read input LFNs from a text file instead of resolving XRootD inputs from the
analysis samples.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT_FILE\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIOUTPUT_FILE\fR
Set the base output ROOT filename.
Each planned output is given a deterministic sample and job-number suffix.
This option is required.
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-dir\fR \fIOUTPUT_DIR\fR
Set the output directory relative to the user's DIRAC catalogue root.
This option is required.
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-se\fR \fISTORAGE_ELEMENT\fR
Override the storage element selected by DIRAC for output data.
.TP
\fB\-\-files\-per\-job\fR \fICOUNT\fR
Derive the number of jobs from the number of input files and the requested
maximum number of files per job.
For XRootD input this overrides sample-level chunk counts.
This option is mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-n\-chunks .
.TP
\fB\-\-n\-chunks\fR \fICOUNT\fR
Request this number of jobs/output chunks for each XRootD sample or across the
complete LFN input list.
For XRootD input this overrides sample-level chunk counts.
The actual number of jobs cannot exceed the number of input files.
This option is mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-files\-per\-job .
.TP
\fB\-\-sample\-name\fR \fINAME\fR
Set the optional sample name passed to workers in LFN input mode.
.TP
\fB\-\-site\fR \fISITE\fR
Restrict the jobs to the named DIRAC computing site.
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR {\fBwms\fR,\fBlocal\fR}
Submit through the DIRAC workload management system or execute through DIRAC
on the submission machine.
The default is
.BR wms .
.TP
.B \-\-ship\-local\-build
Package and ship the active locally built FCCAnalyses installation instead of
using FCCAnalyses from the selected Key4hep stack on the worker.
The active stack must match the stack used to build the local installation.
.TP
\fB\-\-\fR \fIRUN ARGUMENTS\fR
Forward all following arguments unchanged to
.B fccanalysis run
for every planned job.
Their effects therefore apply independently to each job.
Options controlling the per-job input list, output name, sample name, or chunk
planning cannot be forwarded because they are owned by the grid planner.

.SH GRID OUTPUT
Each job registers its ROOT output below
.I OUTPUT_DIR
in the user's DIRAC catalogue namespace.
DIRAC chooses the storage element unless
.B \-\-output\-se
is supplied.
Before submitting a job, the backend checks for its planned output LFN and
removes an existing file to prevent a registration collision.

.SH GRID EXAMPLES
Submit analysis-defined EOS/XRootD samples to the grid:
.nf
fccanalysis submit grid analysis.py \e
    --output result.root --output-dir analyses/example
.fi
.PP
Create ten jobs per XRootD sample and restrict them to one DIRAC site:
.nf
fccanalysis submit grid analysis.py \e
    --output result.root --output-dir analyses/example \e
    --n-chunks 10 --site LCG.Example.org
.fi
.PP
Submit a list of DIRAC LFNs in groups of five files:
.nf
fccanalysis submit grid analysis.py --lfn-input inputs.txt \e
    --output result.root --output-dir analyses/example \e
    --files-per-job 5
.fi
.PP
Pass an event stride to every worker invocation:
.nf
fccanalysis submit grid analysis.py \e
    --output result.root --output-dir analyses/example -- --stride 10
.fi

